Sat Oct 31 11:47:00 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Require typing_extensions at build and run time: setup.py
  imports torch, which needs it since 2.15.
- Require filelock at build and run time for the same reason.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Oct 29 12:19:36 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 2.11.1 (compatible with torch 2.11 and later):
  * Single py3-none wheel per platform, covering all supported
    CPython versions including free-threaded builds
  * Declare the torch>=2.11 dependency in the wheel metadata
  * Add the Python 3.15 classifier and python_requires>=3.10
  * CUDA: only error on torch/torchaudio CUDA major version
    mismatch; minor mismatches are now allowed

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Aug 21 08:56:25 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package of python-torchaudio 2.11.0:
  * Audio signal processing for PyTorch (CPU-only)
  * Upstream 2.11.0 is the latest release and is documented as
    compatible with later torch versions (Factory python-torch
    2.12.0); there is no 2.12.0 torchaudio tag
  * Builds the C++ extensions (lfilter, RNNT, forced_align,
    overdrive) with USE_CUDA=0; CUDA CTC decoder is not built
  * Set PYTHONPATH so PEP 517 can import tools/setup_helpers

